      "title": "Convolution Basics: Filters, Stride, Padding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Convolution Basics: Filters, Stride, Padding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Convolution Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A small learned ==filter== (kernel) slides over the input",
                "Each output value = **dot product** of filter and patch under it",
                "One filter detects ==one pattern== anywhere",
                "Same weights reused at every position (weight sharing)",
                "Params = `k*k*C_in*C_out` + C_out biases, ==independent of image size=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Output Size, Padding, Stride",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Output = ==floor((N + 2P - K) / S) + 1==",
                "{blue:valid}: no padding, the map shrinks",
                "{green:same}: stride 1, output = input, P = (K-1)/2 for odd K",
                "Stride > 1 **downsamples**"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "N",
                "K",
                "S",
                "P",
                "Output",
                "Name"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "32",
                  "3",
                  "1",
                  "1",
                  "32",
                  "same"
                ],
                [
                  "32",
                  "5",
                  "2",
                  "0",
                  "14",
                  "downsample"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. 1x1 vs 3x3 vs Stacked",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "1x1",
                "3x3",
                "Two 3x3"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Sees",
                  "one pixel",
                  "neighborhood",
                  "5x5 receptive field"
                ],
                [
                  "Does",
                  "mixes channels, changes depth",
                  "local patterns",
                  "same view as 5x5"
                ],
                [
                  "Spatial size",
                  "unchanged",
                  "by K, S, P",
                  "by K, S, P"
                ],
                [
                  "Params",
                  "C_in*C_out",
                  "9C^2",
                  "18C^2 vs 25C^2"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Stack small filters",
              "text": "Two 3x3 convs match one 5x5 view with **fewer parameters** (18C^2 vs 25C^2)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pooling and Feature Maps",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pooling and Feature Maps",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Pooling Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Max pooling==: max of each window, typically 2x2 with stride 2",
                "Keeps the **strongest activation**; halves height and width",
                "==Average pooling==: window mean, smooths the map",
                "==GAP== collapses each channel to one number; replaces big FC heads",
                "No learnable parameters; works **per channel**, so C is unchanged",
                "Adds small ==translation invariance=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pooling vs Alternatives",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Max pool",
                "Avg pool / GAP",
                "Stride-2 conv"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Effect",
                  "keeps sharp features",
                  "smooths",
                  "{green:learnable}"
                ],
                [
                  "Where",
                  "early / middle",
                  "end of net",
                  "anywhere"
                ],
                [
                  "Params",
                  "0",
                  "0",
                  "K*K*C_in*C_out"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Shapes and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "nn.MaxPool2d(2, 2)  # (N,C,H,W)",
                "# (8, 16, 32, 32) -> (8, 16, 16, 16)"
              ],
              "note": "PyTorch is (N,C,H,W); TensorFlow is (N,H,W,C)"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pooling too early or too often loses spatial detail",
                "Segmentation and detection need that detail"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Pooling shrinks **H and W only**, never channels, and has ==zero parameters==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
