    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A conv layer takes 3 input channels and outputs 16 using 3x3 filters. How many parameters does it have on a 32x32 image? On a 224x224 image?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "3*3*3*16 + 16 = ==448==, for both image sizes",
                "The same filter is reused at every position, so image size does not matter"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A plain RNN's recurrent factor is about 0.9 per step. What happens to the gradient over 100 steps, and which fix helps?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "0.9^100 is about 0.00003, so the gradient ==vanishes==",
                "Clipping only helps with exploding gradients; use an ==LSTM or GRU== instead"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You remove positional encodings from a transformer. Why can it no longer tell \"dog bites man\" from \"man bites dog\"?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Attention only compares tokens by content, so it has no notion of order",
                "Both sentences contain the same tokens, so the model sees the same set"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
